WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.814
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Tuesday, October twenty-seventh.

2
00:00:04.814 --> 00:00:07.708
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.708 --> 00:00:12.527
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:12.527 --> 00:00:14.097
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:18.741
The United States has formalized a new Ebola entry rule for air travelers.

6
00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:23.518
Cyclone Arnab is expected to reach India's east coast within the next day.

7
00:00:23.518 --> 00:00:26.292
Saudi Arabia reports more interceptions.

8
00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:30.578
And a new maritime warning covers a vessel on fire in the northern Gulf.

9
00:00:30.578 --> 00:00:31.925
Here's the detail.

10
00:00:31.925 --> 00:00:33.515
US entry first.

11
00:00:33.515 --> 00:00:41.446
Confirmed: the US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention has ordered that, from eleven fifty-nine p.m.

12
00:00:41.446 --> 00:00:51.191
Eastern on November third, every passenger boarding a flight to or through the United States must attest that they have not been in the Democratic Republic of the Congo in the previous twenty-one days.

13
00:00:51.191 --> 00:00:57.385
That includes US citizens, charter flights, and a stop at a Congolese airport without getting off.

14
00:00:57.385 --> 00:00:59.890
Airlines must deny boarding without it.

15
00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:02.843
The order was published in the Federal Register today.

16
00:01:02.843 --> 00:01:13.702
Separately, the CDC says non-US citizens, including green card holders, who were in Uganda or South Sudan in the past twenty-one days are not being allowed to enter.

17
00:01:13.702 --> 00:01:21.192
US citizens from those countries are routed through Washington Dulles, Atlanta or New York JFK for screening and monitoring.

18
00:01:21.192 --> 00:01:26.212
Reported: Congo's government says confirmed infections have passed ten thousand.

19
00:01:26.212 --> 00:01:32.572
For teams rotating out of the region, plan around the twenty-one day clock before booking US-bound travel.

20
00:01:32.572 --> 00:01:33.502
India.

21
00:01:33.502 --> 00:01:40.497
Confirmed: the India Meteorological Department has issued a red message cyclone warning for the Andhra Pradesh coast.

22
00:01:40.497 --> 00:01:45.424
It expects Cyclone Arnab to cross that coast by late morning Wednesday local time, around one a.m.

23
00:01:45.424 --> 00:01:56.352
Central, as a very severe cyclonic storm, with sustained winds of one hundred twenty-five to one hundred thirty-five kilometers an hour and gusts to one hundred fifty.

24
00:01:56.352 --> 00:01:59.422
It is expected to weaken quickly after landfall.

25
00:01:59.422 --> 00:02:07.112
Reported: Indian media say tens of thousands are being moved to relief camps, and dozens of trains and some flights are cancelled.

26
00:02:07.112 --> 00:02:11.036
Teams on that coast should hold non-essential movement through Thursday.

27
00:02:11.036 --> 00:02:12.402
Saudi Arabia.

28
00:02:12.402 --> 00:02:22.827
Reported: the Saudi-led coalition says it intercepted three ballistic missiles aimed at the Eastern Province and four drones headed south early Tuesday, with no casualties.

29
00:02:22.827 --> 00:02:27.135
Saudi civil defense issued alerts, then said the danger had passed.

30
00:02:27.135 --> 00:02:30.939
Claim only: the Houthis say they hit several Saudi sites, including an air base.

31
00:02:30.939 --> 00:02:35.052
There is no Saudi confirmation of damage.

32
00:02:35.052 --> 00:02:36.880
At Riyadh's main airport, Flightradar twenty-four data at about five thirty a.m.

33
00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:46.764
Central showed sixty-nine cancellations, about twenty-three percent of roughly three hundred flights scheduled today.

34
00:02:46.764 --> 00:02:51.994
Today's schedule is much smaller than yesterday's, so this is not a like-for-like comparison.

35
00:02:51.994 --> 00:02:55.425
It remains a partial reopening with observed disruption.

36
00:02:55.425 --> 00:02:56.351
Shipping.

37
00:02:56.351 --> 00:03:07.178
Reported: the UK Maritime Trade Operations center has issued a warning after third-party reports of a vessel on fire about sixty-three nautical miles off southern Iraq on Monday.

38
00:03:07.178 --> 00:03:10.422
Cause, crew status and damage are unknown.

39
00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:13.495
UKMTO lists it as suspicious activity, not a confirmed attack.

40
00:03:13.495 --> 00:03:18.707
No newer multinational threat update was found this cycle.

41
00:03:18.707 --> 00:03:20.455
The latest, from Sunday, rates the Strait of Hormuz threat as severe.

42
00:03:20.455 --> 00:03:26.951
A lack of new confirmed attacks does not mean the threat has eased.

43
00:03:26.951 --> 00:03:28.413
Operations check.

44
00:03:28.413 --> 00:03:42.229
Internet and telecom: Georgia Tech's outage measurements show Crimea's connectivity signal dropping overnight to about eighty-five percent of its reference level, and Sevastopol's below eighty percent, with an alert active at the last reading.

45
00:03:42.229 --> 00:03:44.170
The cause is not established.

46
00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:50.566
Russia's digital ministry says mobile internet in central Moscow may be restricted by day through Thursday.

47
00:03:50.566 --> 00:03:56.532
Power: Crimea's Russian-installed grid operator reports consumption limits across the peninsula.

48
00:03:56.532 --> 00:04:00.177
Sudan's state power company says drone strikes on Monday blacked out its southeastern grid.

49
00:04:00.177 --> 00:04:02.262
Restoration is not confirmed.

50
00:04:02.262 --> 00:04:10.044
Borders: Britain has updated its Ethiopia advice for increased tensions and armed groups.

51
00:04:10.044 --> 00:04:11.837
Other domains as above.

52
00:04:11.837 --> 00:04:13.336
That's today's brief.

53
00:04:13.336 --> 00:04:16.155
Current as of five fifty-five a.m.

54
00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:17.060
Central, Tuesday.

55
00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:19.513
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

56
00:04:19.513 --> 00:04:24.011
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

57
00:04:24.011 --> 00:04:26.475
Check the original source before you act.

58
00:04:26.475 --> 00:04:35.550
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

59
00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.324
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

60
00:04:38.324 --> 00:04:39.550
Thanks for listening.
